A||||12||8Ball||Car dieing and hard to start :(||||1||
Z||000000||8Ball||12-19-2001||09:10 PM||||Ok yesterday my car began out of the blue being hard to start. I would have to keep the key turned for about 10-15 seconds before it would turn over. Now it is still doing this, but If I press the gas anymore than just a hair at a time it will die. Or it will backfire and die. I checked my plug wires and they are all on good.<P>Now the car has had a hunting idle for a while now. Well ever since I got it running for the first time. I have yet to figure this one out. Maybe that has something to do with it? The idle will bounce from 800-1000 any time I am sitting still.<P>Anyone have any ideas?<BR>Thanks,<BR>E.B.||||reg||1
Z||000001||Pyric||12-19-2001||10:30 PM||||luckily that doesn't seem like the idle is hunting that much.  Mine used to hunt between 1000 and 1700 until I fixed it.  <P>You might want to check the output voltage on the ignition coil, but the first thing I would do is see if the computer stored any codes.<P>------------------<BR>    <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/fieronegS.jpg">   <P><BR>"Never offend people with style when you can offend them with substance." <BR>--Sam Brown||||reg||1
Z||000002||G-Nasty||12-20-2001||01:15 AM||||Ignition or gas problems will be your best bet. Change fuel filter and check coil. Replace ign module if your budget will afford it. Twice this has happened to me but it was a bad spark plug wire...||||reg||1
Z||000003||SKIDMARK||12-20-2001||01:15 AM||||Things to check would be:<BR>EGR valve and associated vacuum lines. There is a diaphram in the valve body that goes bad, the needle valve gets clogged or stuck with carbon.<BR>Idle air (bypass) valve. This also gets clogged with carbon or stuck.<BR>Check for a bad vacuum leak around the mainfolds and in all the vacuum lines.<BR>As mentioned above, a good place to start is to check trouble codes.||||reg||1
Z||000004||8Ball||12-20-2001||07:01 PM||||Well I haven't been able to check anything on my car yet. But it will no longer start.<P>If I can get away from work early enough tomorrow I will check some things out. I was told today by the service manager at Pontiac that it could also be the TPS, so I guess I will have to get the codes and see what they say.<P>Thanks everyone,<BR>E.B.||||reg||1
Z||000005||JohnF||12-20-2001||07:11 PM|||| <BLOCKQUOTE><font size="1" face="Verdana, Arial, Helvetica">quote:</font><HR>Originally posted by 8Ball:<BR><B> ...so I guess I will have to get the codes and see what they say.<BR>E.B.</B><HR></BLOCKQUOTE><P>You have an ENGINE light but haven't posted the codes?  Shame, shame.  <P>Give us the codes, then let us figure it out even if there aren't any.  That is also a clue!<P>||||reg||10
Z||000006||8Ball||12-20-2001||09:30 PM||||No I didn't have a check engine light, But thought I would check anyway. I tried to check I shorted the two top pins on the passenger side. Only thing that happened was my light blinked twice. I didn't even get the code 12 3 times.<BR>Why is this?||||reg||1
Z||000007||8Ball||12-21-2001||07:15 AM||||bump||||reg||1
Z||000008||conductor||12-21-2001||07:45 AM||||Hi I had the same problem and let a mechanic search for it(after I had push the F from a crossroads(?) to a parkinglot.<BR>Turned out to be a very bad cap and rotor.<BR>He cleaned it and sort of protected it agains moisture with a film of spray and it idles like a kitten now.<BR>I ordered the new stuff at <A HREF="http://www.fierostore.com" TARGET=_blank>www.fierostore.com</A>   <BR>Grtx Richard.||||reg||1
Z||000009||84Bill||12-21-2001||10:09 AM||||Sounds like the starter solenoid is sticking. take it off and spray wd40 in there. The stalling may be a timing problem particularly if it barfs out the intake.||||reg||1
Z||000010||8Ball||12-21-2001||06:21 PM||||Well I have a new rotor and cap so shouldn't be that. I will check the solonoid tomorrow when I have some light. I just hope it is a little warmer tomorrow.<BR>Thanks for the suggestions guys<P>E.B.||||reg||1
Z||000011||thomas_l||12-22-2001||08:30 AM||||That's an awful lot of diagnostic advice not even knowing what year/engine. Before you buy any more parts invest in a spark tester (looks like a spark plug with an alligator clip soldered to it) and a cheap digital voltmeter (I've seen them for &lt;$35 at Pep Boys). Diagnose the ignition first because its usually easiest. If you have a good spark at the right time then diagnose fuel. You might need a cheap fuel pressure gauge, but since you're not running pressure should be pretty easy to guess. Even with a bad sensor somewhere, if you have fuel and fire at the right time, the engine will at least run badly.<P>Too bad you are 4 hours away otherwise I would give you a hand. Maybe someone on here that's in the Knoxville area can provide some help in person...<P>(edit: 8Ball you have a PM)<p>[This message has been edited by thomas_l (edited 12-22-2001).]||||reg||1
Z||000012||85 gt fiero||12-22-2001||11:08 AM||||I would check the ignition coil and module, and i would also check the egr(my car had the same problem and it turned out to be the egr.)  hope you get it fixed.  randy<P>------------------<BR>RALLY CAR, FULL ROLL CAGE, SKID PLATES, LIGHT BARS, SCS SUSPENSION, KONI ADJUSTERS,HIGH POINT CUTOFFS, AND BRIGHT YELLOW||||reg||1
